WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:09.198
With each visit to the Upper World, the Little Mermaid grew more unhappy.

2
00:00:09.199 --> 00:00:15.374
"The Prince’s world is so much bigger than mine," said the mermaid to herself.

3
00:00:15.375 --> 00:00:19.480
"Humans can walk on land and sail the seas.

4
00:00:19.481 --> 00:00:25.698
Their lives are so exciting, and my life is so boring."

5
00:00:25.699 --> 00:00:32.901
The Little Mermaid thought about how she’d like to live in the Upper World rather than the Sea Kingdom.

6
00:00:32.902 --> 00:00:37.164
Day after day she sat in her garden, alone.

7
00:00:37.165 --> 00:00:42.493
Her sisters became worried and went to their grandmother.

8
00:00:42.494 --> 00:00:48.333
"Grandmother," said the eldest sister, "please talk to the Little Mermaid.

9
00:00:48.334 --> 00:00:52.119
Find out why she’s so gloomy."

10
00:00:52.120 --> 00:00:58.665
So the Wise Mermaid went to her grandchild and took the Little Mermaid in her arms.

11
00:00:58.666 --> 00:01:03.729
"Sweet one, tell me what is bothering you."

12
00:01:03.730 --> 00:01:09.839
"Grandmother," said the Little Mermaid, "what happens to humans if they don’t drown?

13
00:01:09.840 --> 00:01:12.116
Do they live forever?"

14
00:01:12.117 --> 00:01:16.572
"I told you," the Wise Mermaid answered.

15
00:01:16.573 --> 00:01:23.578
"They die much sooner than we do, but their souls live forever."

16
00:01:23.579 --> 00:01:25.647
"I want a soul too.

17
00:01:25.648 --> 00:01:29.344
And I want to live in the Upper World."

18
00:01:29.345 --> 00:01:34.074
"Your place is here," said the Wise Mermaid.

19
00:01:34.075 --> 00:01:40.403
"Believe me, there is no better spot in the world than the Sea Kingdom.

20
00:01:40.404 --> 00:01:43.432
We are all very happy here.

21
00:01:43.433 --> 00:01:46.904
It is our home."

22
00:01:46.905 --> 00:01:55.672
"But I want a soul like my Prince, so we can both live forever together," the Little Mermaid said stubbornly.

23
00:01:55.673 --> 00:02:01.852
"You don’t need a soul," replied the Wise Mermaid, annoyed.

24
00:02:01.853 --> 00:02:07.179
"As a mermaid you will live for a very long time.

25
00:02:07.180 --> 00:02:12.051
And when you die, you will become lovely sea foam.

26
00:02:12.052 --> 00:02:18.595
This way you will remain part of the sea and a part of all of us."

27
00:02:18.596 --> 00:02:25.653
The Little Mermaid pleaded, "Please, Grandmother, tell me how I can get a soul."

28
00:02:25.654 --> 00:02:31.313
The Wise Mermaid saw that she could not change her granddaughter’s mind.

29
00:02:31.314 --> 00:02:38.888
"Well, I’ve heard that a human and a member of the sea folk must marry," she said.

30
00:02:38.889 --> 00:02:42.932
"Your Prince would have to fall in love with you.

31
00:02:42.933 --> 00:02:50.226
Then, if he married you, you would become truly human and have a soul."

32
00:02:50.227 --> 00:02:56.352
"So all I have to do is marry the Prince?" asked the Little Mermaid hopefully.

33
00:02:56.353 --> 00:03:01.068
"I really do not know," replied the Wise Mermaid.

34
00:03:01.069 --> 00:03:05.945
"What I have told you is only an old tale.

35
00:03:05.946 --> 00:03:12.795
I know of no mermaid who has ever received a soul—or even wanted one.

36
00:03:12.796 --> 00:03:17.345
We live very happily without souls."

37
00:03:17.346 --> 00:03:21.700
But the Little Mermaid did not hear her grandmother’s words.

38
00:03:21.701 --> 00:03:26.801
She was already too busy thinking and making plans.

39
00:03:26.802 --> 00:03:33.207
"Grandmother, what must I do to live in the Upper World?" she asked.

40
00:03:33.208 --> 00:03:37.875
"Forget about such things," said the Wise Mermaid.

41
00:03:37.876 --> 00:03:42.429
"You would need legs and feet to live there."

42
00:03:42.430 --> 00:03:45.916
She patted her granddaughter on the head.

43
00:03:45.917 --> 00:03:52.938
"Your beautiful tail makes it impossible for you to live on land."

44
00:03:52.939 --> 00:03:58.189
The Little Mermaid looked unhappily at her body and sighed.

45
00:03:58.190 --> 00:04:01.009
"I hate my tail."

46
00:04:01.010 --> 00:04:06.186
The Wise Mermaid shook her head and said, "You are lovely.

47
00:04:06.187 --> 00:04:08.792
Now go and play.

48
00:04:08.793 --> 00:04:12.522
Stop thinking about the Upper World."

49
00:04:12.523 --> 00:04:17.081
The Little Mermaid swam away, but she didn’t play.

50
00:04:17.082 --> 00:04:22.147
She thought, "There must be some way to fulfill my dream.

51
00:04:22.148 --> 00:04:25.023
Someone must have the knowledge I need.

52
00:04:25.024 --> 00:04:33.322
Maybe I’ll ask the Sea Witch for help."

